<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ibe16dacfbb4463f9dd0012710b01795344dcb663" commit="44930027d1672d94eb901c0a75d32de2949bfaaa" commit_message="BACKPORT: memory: mediatek: Add SMI driver  This patch add SMI(Smart Multimedia Interface) driver. This driver is responsible to enable/disable iommu and control the power domain and clocks of each local arbiter.  Signed-off-by: Yong Wu &lt;yong.wu@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Matthias Brugger &lt;matthias.bgg@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit cc8bbe1a83128ad06457e4dc69907c4f9a6fc1a7)  [yong.wu: this patch synchronizes the FROMLIST commit:  &lt;6aaee7c FROMLIST: memory: mediatek: Add SMI driver&gt;  in chromeos-3.18 with the UPSTREAM version.]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot to UI on oak-rev4 TEST=http://videojs.com/  Change-Id: Ibe16dacfbb4463f9dd0012710b01795344dcb663 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331165 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331165" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/331165/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3686fc1384c30023f90c9d109ea17ce3e0852c32" commit="d89b0643f88cdfef3142ed415c5063000bbba81b" commit_message="BACKPORT: iommu/mediatek: Add mt8173 IOMMU driver  This patch adds support for mediatek m4u (MultiMedia Memory Management Unit).  Signed-off-by: Yong Wu &lt;yong.wu@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Robin Murphy &lt;robin.murphy@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 0df4fabe208d9576f2671d31e77cf46d20fdcd01)  [yong.wu: this patch synchronizes the FROMLIST commit:  &lt;ade9461 CHROMIUM: iommu/mediatek: Add missing include file&gt;  &lt;7313d3f FROMLIST: iommu/mediatek: Add mt8173 IOMMU driver&gt;  in chromeos-3.18 with the UPSTREAM version.  Note that: this commit is not changed here.  &lt;665e797 FROMLIST: iommu/mediatek: Add 4GB mode support&gt;]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot to UI on oak-rev4 TEST=http://videojs.com/  Change-Id: I3686fc1384c30023f90c9d109ea17ce3e0852c32 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331166 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331166" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/331166/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If603f7e6a97772a97f587480de114b87ff4df75b" commit="d1a1a1181a0e4c2141483f8fa1d5f664867fd373" commit_message="UPSTREAM: iommu/mediatek: Select ARM_DMA_USE_IOMMU  The newly added Mediatek IOMMU driver uses the IOMMU_DMA infrastructure, but unlike other such drivers, it does not select 'ARM_DMA_USE_IOMMU', which is a prerequisite, leading to a link error:  warning: (MTK_IOMMU) selects IOMMU_DMA which has unmet direct dependencies (IOMMU_SUPPORT &amp;&amp; NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH) drivers/iommu/built-in.o: In function `iommu_put_dma_cookie': mtk_iommu.c:(.text+0x11fe): undefined reference to `put_iova_domain' drivers/iommu/built-in.o: In function `iommu_dma_init_domain': mtk_iommu.c:(.text+0x1316): undefined reference to `init_iova_domain' drivers/iommu/built-in.o: In function `__iommu_dma_unmap': mtk_iommu.c:(.text+0x1380): undefined reference to `find_iova'  This adds the same select that the other drivers have. On a related note, I wonder if we should just always select ARM_DMA_USE_IOMMU whenever any IOMMU driver is enabled. Are there any cases where we would enable an IOMMU but not use it?  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot to UI on oak-rev4 TEST=http://videojs.com/  Signed-off-by: Arnd Bergmann &lt;arnd@arndb.de&gt; Fixes: 0df4fabe208d (&quot;iommu/mediatek: Add mt8173 IOMMU driver&quot;) Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 1928832f0241f0c39fcd2ce73aaa39d37db50a97) Signed-off-by: Yong Wu &lt;yong.wu@mediatek.com&gt;  Change-Id: If603f7e6a97772a97f587480de114b87ff4df75b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331167 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331167" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/67/331167/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1b7c3a6e85690cadc1c3b4539f8db4d2f98ecf64" commit="11ff51eb1b3be81696e6fe327efe34b37906bf1f" commit_message="UPSTREAM: iommu/mediatek: Mark PM functions as __maybe_unused  When CONFIG_PM is unset, we get a harmless warning for this driver:  drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c:665:12: error: 'mtk_iommu_suspend' defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function] drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c:680:12: error: 'mtk_iommu_resume' defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]  Marking the functions as __maybe_unused gits rid of the two functions and lets the compiler silently drop the object code, while still doing syntax checking on them for build-time verification.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot to UI on oak-rev4 TEST=http://videojs.com/  Signed-off-by: Arnd Bergmann &lt;arnd@arndb.de&gt; Fixes: 0df4fabe208d (&quot;iommu/mediatek: Add mt8173 IOMMU driver&quot;) Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit fd99f796a20b1a805c80ee51d7349d65103e7aaf) Signed-off-by: Yong Wu &lt;yong.wu@mediatek.com&gt;  Change-Id: I1b7c3a6e85690cadc1c3b4539f8db4d2f98ecf64 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331168 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331168" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/68/331168/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If7cfdf61e1eec608b4aa208c12e77126d1d801da" commit="82c961199802bf8bee5809caa92ac4d2234b36c9" commit_message="UPSTERAM: iommu/dma: Fix NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH dependency  IOMMU_DMA does indeed depend on scatterlists having a DMA length, but the NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH symbol should be selected, not depended upon.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot to UI on oak-rev4 TEST=http://videojs.com/  Reported-by: Arnd Bergmann &lt;arnd@arndb.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Robin Murphy &lt;robin.murphy@arm.com&gt; Acked-by: Arnd Bergmann &lt;arnd@arndb.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 59a68eb892497d32493a1fcbc4bd8f1ce13f598f) Signed-off-by: Yong Wu &lt;yong.wu@mediatek.com&gt;  Change-Id: If7cfdf61e1eec608b4aa208c12e77126d1d801da Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331169 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331169" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" p